Project Name:
Professional-Level Cloud Web Application
What is it (short):
It is a full-stack cloud-based application architecture that includes all major components needed to run a modern web app:
Frontend → User interface (what users see)
Backend API → Handles logic & requests
Database → Stores data
Load Balancer → Distributes traffic
Networking → Connects services securely
Infrastructure (Infra) → Cloud resources (servers, storage, etc.)

2.
Project Name:
Smart Serverless Automation Pipeline
What is it (short):
It is a serverless cloud workflow where tasks are automated without managing servers.

Flow:
S3 / Blob Storage → Stores files/data
Lambda / Azure Functions → Runs code automatically (no server needed)
Data Processing → Processes uploaded data
DynamoDB / Cosmos DB → Stores processed data
CloudWatch / Azure Monitor → Tracks system & sends alerts

3.
Project Name:
Enterprise-Grade Kubernetes Deployment
What is it (short):
It is a production-level deployment system where applications are run using containers and managed automatically at scale.
Main Components:
Docker → Packages app into containers
Kubernetes → Manages and runs containers
Terraform → Creates infrastructure using code
Auto-scaling → Automatically increases/decreases resources








1. Production-Grade Disaster Recovery Platform ✅
Build a disaster recovery solution that automatically backs up critical infrastructure and application data, with a defined RPO/RTO strategy and the ability to restore services during a regional or infrastructure failure.

Tech: AWS, Terraform, S3, EBS Snapshots, Route53, RDS, CloudWatch, Lambda

2. Zero-Downtime Blue/Green Deployment Platform✅

Build a deployment platform that maintains two production environments and allows you to safely release new application versions with instant traffic switching and rollback capabilities.

Tech: AWS ALB, EC2/ECS/EKS, Terraform, Docker, GitHub Actions, Route53

3. Canary Deployment Platform✅

Implement progressive application deployments where a small percentage of users receive the new version first, allowing you to monitor performance and gradually increase traffic before a full rollout.

Tech: Kubernetes, Istio, Argo Rollouts, Prometheus, Grafana, ArgoCD, Helm

4. Centralized Logging & Observability Platform✅

Build a centralized logging platform that collects logs from applications, containers, and Kubernetes workloads, making it easy to search, analyze, and troubleshoot production issues.

Tech: Kubernetes, Fluent Bit, Elasticsearch/OpenSearch, Kibana/OpenSearch Dashboards, Prometheus, Grafana

5. Multi-Region High Availability Infrastructure✅

Build a multi-region AWS infrastructure capable of handling regional failures with automated traffic routing, replicated data, health checks, and failover mechanisms.

Tech: AWS, Terraform, Route53, CloudFront, S3, RDS, ALB, Auto Scaling, IAM